{
  // The dashboard's *browser* half. DOM lib, and `types: []` so Node's globals
  // are genuinely absent rather than merely discouraged — a custom element that
  // reaches for `process` should not compile.
  //
  // This is also what makes the claim about typed projections true rather than
  // aspirational: the app imports `ExecutionDetail` and `isStuck` from the
  // engine's `protocol` entry rather than restating them, so a field added to a
  // projection is a compile error here. Nothing checked this code at all before
  // a config existed for it, so that error had nowhere to appear.
  // `module`/`moduleResolution` are overridden because the root config is
  // CommonJS for the Node half, and this half is neither: it is ESM source that
  // esbuild bundles into an IIFE, so the module system is the bundler's problem
  // and never reaches a browser. Inheriting CommonJS here would also break
  // resolution of `workflow-engine/protocol` and of `lit`, which is ESM-only.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "Bundler",
    "types": []
  },
  "include": ["**/*.ts"]
}
